#X text 82 626 0: messages (see Messages below) \; 1: signal \, external FM modulator (fms 2 \, see FM), f 64;
#X obj 60 686 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 710 0: signal left \; 1: signal right \; 2: events: value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 786 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 810 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. har1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. cut 60 (see the settings blocks below) \; delay flanger / chorus1 / chorus2 / slap / long / off \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices \, times bnd semitones \; n <name> <0-127>: a setting from a pot \, CV or MIDI CC \, \;   scaled to its range (switches in zones \, 64 = 0 if bipolar) \; nget <name> <tag>: outlet 3 gets norm <tag> <0-127> \, \;   the setting as a pot position (for pickup) \; disp <name>: outlet 3 gets disp <label> <value> \, \;   two symbols for a display (OLED) \; oled <host> <port>: changed settings to O2O (an OLED) as \;   OSC \, sent from a thread of its own \; oledtext <line 1> <line 2>: two lines for the OLED \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly, f 64;
#X obj 60 1206 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1230 0 har1 (45): Timbre of DCO1 \, one knob through all 15 distinct original timbres \, dark to bright: 0 16' / 9-64 saw net (16'2' \, 16'4'2' \, 16'4' \, 16'8'4' \, all at 45 \, 16'8'2' \, 16'8') / 73-127 square net (16'8' \, 16'8'4' \, 16'4' \, 16'4'2' \, all \, 16'8'2' \, 16'2'). One foot or the net per step \, no jumps. Combinations without 16' = oct1 2-4. \; 1 har2 (45): Timbre of DCO2 \, same path. \; 2 env1 (0): Envelope of DCO1 (DEG1) \, one knob: 0 gate / 1 very short pluck (no fade from the gate) / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. -1 = own values a1 ... r1. \; 3 env2 (0): Envelope of DCO2 (DEG2) \, the same \, -1 = own values a2 ... r2. \; 4 intv (0): Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 in semitones \, 0-12 \, as stored on the Poly-800 II. \; 5 detn (0): Detune of DCO2 downwards: the original's 4 steps 0 \, 6.5 \, 13 \, 26 cents lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, 127. \; 6 lev1 (127): Level of DCO1. \; 7 lev2 (0): Level of DCO2 (every voice has both DCOs). Above full scale (lev1 + lev2 > 127) both are scaled down together., f 64;
#X obj 60 1578 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Timbre\ (har1\ /\ har2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1602 The 15 distinct timbres of the original \, dark to bright: \; 0: 16' / saw net 9: 16'2' / 18: 16'4'2' / 27: 16'4' / \; 36: 16'8'4' / 45: all / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: 16'8' / \; square net 73: 16'8' / 82: 16'8'4' / 91: 16'4' / \; 100: 16'4'2' / 109: all / 118: 16'8'2' / 127: 16'2'. \; One foot or the net per step. The combinations without 16' \; are the same waves higher: use oct1 / oct2 2-4. \; A fading foot rises in power \, so the morph has no dips., f 64;
#X obj 60 1758 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1782 Two read-only lists send presets to the object \, changing \; slots never writes anything back. Both send 'dump pdoly8 ...' \; messages (here via [s] \, nothing is wired across the patch). \; [p8factory]: the 64 Poly-800 II factory programs \, slot 0-63 \; (0 = program 11 \, 7 = 18 \, 8 = 21 ... 63 = 88) \, read from \; presets/poly800mk2-factory.txt next to the abstraction. \; [p8user name]: your own sounds in a [text define -k name] \; (saved with the patch). A slot number recalls\; only \; 'store N' writes: it stores the current sound in slot N \; (it needs outlet 2 of pdoly8~ at its right inlet \, here \; via [s]/[r]). 'write file' / 'read file' on the text \; define save and load banks. tools/p8sysex.py converts \; Poly-800 II sysex dumps to preset text and back., f 64;
#X floatatom 82 2000 4 0 63 0 factory - -;
#X obj 82 2030 p8factory;
